      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it's actually quite readable. Thanks for not overdoing it.\n\nI've actually been tasked with getting the documentation's structural density score up a bit for the engineering review board. The current draft is a little on the \"thin\" side according to the linter. Can you expand this? I need more detail on things like error handling and rate limiting. \n\nJust a reminder: try to keep it efficient. Don't just add a bunch of fluff or break things up into tiny, useless pieces just to bump the heading and bullet count. I still need it to be a high-quality guide, not a wall of lists.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
